{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-6351-r4513509","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Frog's Legs à la Parisienne","sourcePageId":6351,"sourceRevision":"4513509","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:05:47Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Frog's%20Legs%20%C3%A0%20la%20Parisienne&oldid=4513509","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:20.218Z","sourceCategories":["Category:French recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using frog","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using light cream","Category:Recipes using pepper","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e786a28ed2970a586e5f6bc7a7437b19faf25ec5a2eeb77c8a5514cbd5d85ebf","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Meat recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of France|Cuisine of France]] | [[Cookbook:Meat and Poultry|Meat]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Onion cream sauce ===\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n*1 ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] light [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] salt\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*1 tbsp minced [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], well-beaten\n\n=== Cooking ===\n*16 large [[Cookbook:Frog|frog]] legs\n*Boiling water\n*Juice of ½ [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] each of [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]] and [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]s, well-beaten\n*Fine dry [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|bread crumbs]]\n*[[Cookbook:Fat|Fat]], for deep frying\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Onion cream sauce ===\n# Melt the butter in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] over medium heat.\n# Stir flour into melted butter. Cook for a few minutes, stirring, until the mixture loses its floury taste. Do not let the mixture brown.\n# Gradually stir the cream into the flour mixture, taking care to prevent lumps. Cook, stirring, until mixture has thickened.\n# Mix in the salt, onion, and parsley.\n# [[Cookbook:Tempering|Temper]] the beaten egg with some of the sauce, taking care not to curdle the egg. Stir this mixture back into the sauce.\n# Remove from heat and let cool slightly.\n\n=== Cooking ===\n#[[Cookbook:Blanching|Blanch]] frog legs in boiling water with lemon juice and salt and pepper. \n#Drain legs and pat dry.\n#Dip legs into eggs and roll in bread crumbs. [[Cookbook:Deep Fry|Deep fry]] at 370°F (190°C) for 2 to 3 minutes until legs are tender (check the temperature of the fat with a [[Cookbook:Thermometer|thermometer]]).\n#Serve with onion cream sauce.\n\n[[fr:Livre de cuisine/Cuisses de grenouilles à l'ail et au persil]]\n\n[[Category:French recipes|Frog's Legs à la Parisienne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using frog|Frog Legs à la Parisienne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using light cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[